# Forge special cases

Everything with a recipe goes through `just` (`just --list`). This skill covers the rest.

**Rule: do not guess flags.** Before using a subcommand that is not written out below, run `{% if platform == 'github' %}gh{% else %}fj{% endif %} <command> --help` once and use what it says.
{%- if platform == 'github' %}

The commands below were checked against `gh --help` (2.46.0), not run against GitHub.

## Labels

```bash
gh label list
gh label create "area/api" --color 1d76db --description "API surface"
gh issue edit 12 --add-label "bug,area/api" --remove-label "triage"
gh pr edit 34 --add-label "bug"
```

## Issue types

Issue types (Bug, Feature, Task, …) are defined per organisation. `gh` 2.46.0 has no flag for them, so they go through the API. Not run against GitHub — if a call fails, check `gh --version` and `gh issue edit --help` for a `--type` flag first.

```bash
gh api "orgs/{owner}/issue-types" --jq '.[].name'               # types that exist
gh api "repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/12" --jq '.type.name'       # type of an issue
gh api -X PATCH "repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/12" -f type=Bug    # set it
```

Set the type when opening an issue: `just issue-new` first, then the PATCH call with the new number.

## Dependencies

There is no CLI support. State the dependency in the issue body (`Blocked by #12`) so it is visible and linked.

## Closing an issue

Issues close when a PR with `Closes #N` is merged. To close one without a PR:

```bash
gh issue close 12 --comment "Superseded by #15"
```
{%- else %}

Tested with forgejo-cli (`fj`) 0.7.0. Check `fj version`; with a different version, verify with `--help` first.

**Always pass the host:** `fj -H "$(just _forge-host)" …`. Without it fj cannot tell which repository is meant when there are several remotes or the branch has no upstream.

## Labels

```bash
fj -H "$(just _forge-host)" repo labels view
fj -H "$(just _forge-host)" repo labels create "area/api" 1d76db --description "API surface"
fj -H "$(just _forge-host)" issue edit 12 labels --add bug --add area/api --rm triage
fj -H "$(just _forge-host)" pr edit 34 labels --add bug
```

## Dependencies

```bash
fj -H "$(just _forge-host)" issue depend add 15 12     # 15 depends on 12
fj -H "$(just _forge-host)" issue depend list 15
fj -H "$(just _forge-host)" issue depend remove 15 12
```

`depend remove` in fj 0.7.0 prints `Error: unexpected status code 201 Created` and exits non-zero although the dependency is removed. Confirm with `depend list` instead of retrying.

## Closing an issue

Issues close when a PR with `Closes #N` is merged. To close one without a PR:

```bash
fj -H "$(just _forge-host)" issue close 12 --with-msg "Superseded by #15"
```
{%- endif %}

## Not here on purpose

Merging, approving, deleting branches or releases, and changing repository settings are the human's.
